-- Bug #955, the rule's soundness carve-out: a later CREATE OR MODIFY.
--
-- POSITIVE TEST — this script is EXPECTED to PASS `mxcli check`.
--
-- Read the reason carefully, because it is NOT the reason
-- 955-forward-definition-order-tolerated.mdl passes. That file holds references
-- `exec` genuinely tolerates. This one does not: run against a project that
-- does not already have Ord.Mutable, `mxcli exec` fails here exactly as it does
-- for a plain CREATE ("entity 'Ord.Mutable' not found for parameter 'T'").
--
-- MDL-ORDER01 stays silent anyway, because it runs WITHOUT a project and cannot
-- know. A plain CREATE asserts the document does not exist yet — that is what
-- makes the rule sound with nothing to look at. `CREATE OR MODIFY` asserts
-- nothing: the entity may already be in the project, in which case the forward
-- reference resolves and the script is correct. Flagging it would reject
-- working scripts, so the case is left to `--references`, which can look.
--
-- The residue is deliberate and known: with a later CREATE OR MODIFY and no -p,
-- `check` still does not predict this exec failure.

create module Ord;

create microflow Ord.Modifier (
  $T: Ord.Mutable
)
returns String as $Out
begin
  declare $Out String = 'x';
  return $Out;
end;

create or modify persistent entity Ord.Mutable ( Name: String(100) );
